{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "06", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "11", "M": "48", "S": "06"}}, "news": [{"title": "Pimpri Chinchwad civic body likely to record low property tax collection compared to previous two years", "para": "The Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation predicts a dip in property tax revenues for the upcoming fiscal year. In a bid to enhance collection rates, heightened enforcement actions have been initiated. Political candidates and residents in red zones are responding positively to various incentives offered. To further the recovery process, over eighty non-residential properties have been seized by tax authorities, and water supply cut-offs are being implemented.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/pimpri-chinchwad-civic-body-likely-to-record-low-property-tax-collection-compared-to-previous-two-years/133831407?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-84804/133831407.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Chandigarh scraps mandatory no-dues certificate for leasehold property sale", "para": "The Chandigarh administration has eliminated the requirement for a no-dues certificate, streamlining the process of selling leasehold properties in the Union Territory. This amendment, championed by the Property Consultants Association Chandigarh, significantly accelerates real estate transactions. As a result, buyers, sellers, and consultants can expect a smoother experience with reduced administrative hold-ups.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/chandigarh-scraps-mandatory-no-dues-certificate-for-leasehold-property-sale/133831602?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-80092/133831602.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "CBI books Essel Group chairman Subhash Chandra, others over alleged \u20b91,322 crore LICHFL loan loss", "para": "Subhash Chandra, along with eight others, is under scrutiny as the CBI has registered an FIR accusing them of inflating their net worth to secure loans fraudulently. This situation has led LIC Housing Finance to announce a staggering loss exceeding \u20b91,322 crore. The Directorate of Enforcement will also step in with a money laundering investigation, and those accused can expect to be questioned soon about these dubious financial activities.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/housing-finance/cbi-books-essel-group-chairman-subhash-chandra-others-over-alleged-1322-crore-lichfl-loan-loss/133831548?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-150482/133831548.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "housing-finance"}]}